+    """Construct the system prompt split into two cacheable blocks.
+
+    The first block contains the static coaching *instructions* which never change
+    between requests – it is byte‑stable and can stay hot in the cache.
+
+    The second block contains the *volatile* per‑athlete context (date, profile,
+    zones, goal, long‑term facts, language).  This part changes when a fact is
+    saved, so it is allowed to be re‑cached without evicting the static block.
+
+    Both blocks use ``cache_control: {"type": "ephemeral"}`` – Anthropic permits up
+    to four markers per request, and two is sufficient here.
+    """
+    # Block 1 – static instructions (byte‑stable).
+    instructions_block = {"type": "text", "text": INSTRUCTIONS, "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}}
+    # Block 2 – volatile per‑user tail.
+    tail_text = athlete_context(a, today)
+    tail_block = {"type": "text", "text": tail_text, "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}}
+    return [instructions_block, tail_block]
+
 
